// Brute's "Knockback Mastery" Hero Traits - a themed batch of 4 ordinary Passive Upgrades (Ground
// Pound/Crushing Blow/Lasting Impact/Overwhelming Force), independent of Protector Aura/Juggernaut
// itself, built on generic hooks (a player-wide landing signal, the shared Stun/knockback pipeline)
// rather than anything Juggernaut- or Protector-Aura-specific. See
// BruteKnockbackMasterySystem.cs/docs/brute-knockback-mastery.md.

// Ground Pound - on landing (see PlayerMovement.qtn's OnPlayerLanded, fired from AutoJumpSystem)
// from at least MinFallDistance of net drop, pulses a pure knockback burst (BruteKnockbackMasterySystem
// applies it directly rather than going through HitEffectUtility.ApplyShockwave - see that system's
// own comment for why: this needed its own dedicated view event to resolve Source's BlastEffectPrefab,
// and ApplyShockwave always fires the generic ShockwaveReleased alongside it, which would double up
// the VFX). Force/UpwardForce are baked here (not KnockbackTier itself - that's a plain C# enum,
// never declared through qtn, so it can't live on an unmanaged component) at Apply time via the
// shared RuntimeConfig.EffectConfig.GetKnockback (same Small/Medium/Strong bucket every
// KnockbackEffectData in the game already pulls from - see GroundPoundPassiveUpgradeData.Apply),
// so Ground Pound pushes exactly as hard as any other Tier-matched source instead of authoring its
// own bespoke number. Source is baked by GroundPoundPassiveUpgradeData.Apply
// ("upgrade->Source = this;", same self-referencing AssetRef pattern VortexExplodeOnDestroy.Source
// uses) purely so the view can resolve BlastEffectPrefab off the exact asset that granted this.
component GroundPoundUpgrade
{
    FP Radius;
    FP Force;
    FP UpwardForce;
    FP MinFallDistance;
    AssetRef<GroundPoundPassiveUpgradeData> Source;
}

// Crushing Blow - bonus damage vs a currently-Stunned target, read live in DamageUtility.
// ResolveOutgoingDamage via StatusEffectUtility.IsStunned - same shape Max's Hot Target/Pixie's
// Unstable Targeting already use for their own conditional bonuses.
component CrushingBlowUpgrade
{
    FP DamageMultiplierBonus;
}

// Lasting Impact - a Stun Brute himself causes lasts longer, read live inside StatusEffectUtility.
// ApplyStun once it knows the stunning owner - see that method's own comment for why every other
// existing Stun source (Iron Shoulder, Juggernaut landing impact, StunEffectData, Overload) is
// unaffected without this component.
component LastingImpactUpgrade
{
    FP DurationMultiplierBonus;
}
